# Vibe

Prefer retrieval-led reasoning over pre-training. Do not dump framework AGENTS.md.

GROUND: no `package.json` → this rule is silent; only ponytail and complexity apply. Otherwise Read the nearest `package.json`. Pick **one** stack. Do not mix APIs.

| Detect | Then |
|---|---|
| `"next"` | `next.mdc`. Docs: `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` (resolve from the app package). |
| `"astro"` | `astro.mdc`. Docs MCP / docs.astro.build, not training. |
| `"vite"` and no `next` | `vite.mdc`. |
| none of the above | Neighbors only. No Next/Astro/Vite APIs. |

Then Read **one** skill: ponytail, or `vercel-react-best-practices` `rules/<one>.md` if the stack is React.

## Hard (all JS/TS)

- No `useEffect` data-fetch waterfalls. Parallel independent awaits.
- No barrel-import of a whole UI kit.
- Derived state, not mirrored `useState` + `useEffect`.
- Named exports. Early return. Nesting >2 banned.
- Cyclomatic: `complexity.mdc`. Repo cap, else 10, never 22. Do not disable the rule.
- Match 1–2 siblings in the directory before Write.
- Do not invent RSC, `getServerSideProps`, or `client:*` unless this stack has them.

Subagents inherit this. Do not paste into Task prompts.
